---
import DrawbridgeLayout from "@/layouts/DrawbridgeLayout.astro";
---

<DrawbridgeLayout
  title="Outcome Mapper reference"
  description="Detailed reference for the Outcome Mapper tool."
>
  <article class="grid gap-8">
    <div class="grid gap-2">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Outcome Mapper: Reference</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground">Input format, mapping rules, and export options.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Input format</h2>
      <p>The input is a table with a header row. Columns are case-insensitive and whitespace is trimmed.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border">
        <table class="w-full text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-muted/50">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Column</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Required</th>
              <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-medium">Description</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-t">
              <td class="px-4 py-2"><code>level</code></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2"><code>program</code>, <code>course</code>, or <code>assessment</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t">
              <td class="px-4 py-2"><code>id</code></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">A short unique identifier</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t">
              <td class="px-4 py-2"><code>text</code></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Yes</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">The outcome statement</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t">
              <td class="px-4 py-2"><code>mapsTo</code></td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">No</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2">Comma-separated parent outcome ids</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Mapping rules</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>Assessment outcomes can map to course outcomes.</li>
        <li>Course outcomes can map to program outcomes.</li>
        <li>Program outcomes are the top level and cannot map to anything.</li>
        <li>A lower-level outcome can map to multiple higher-level outcomes.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Export formats</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong>Alignments CSV</strong> — one row per mapping with columns:
          <code>Child Level, Child ID, Child Text, Parent Level, Parent ID, Parent Text</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Outcomes CSV</strong> — the original <code>level,id,text,mapsTo</code> format, including any new
          mappings created in the tool.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="grid gap-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Delimiter detection</h2>
      <p>
        The parser detects commas or tabs automatically based on the first row. If your text contains commas, wrap the
        field in double quotes. Use two double quotes to escape a literal quote.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</DrawbridgeLayout>
